      "response": "Photosynthesis is how plants use sunlight to make their own food.\n\nThey take in **water** through their roots and **carbon dioxide** from the air. Their leaves capture sunlight using a green substance called **chlorophyll**.\n\nWith that energy, plants turn water and carbon dioxide into **sugar** for growth. They also release **oxygen** into the air—the gas we breathe.\n\nIn short: **sunlight + water + carbon dioxide → sugar + oxygen**.",
